# Twinkle Twinkle Little Star — ASCII tab test fixture.
#
# Public-domain melody: traditional, popularised via Mozart's K. 265
# variations and Jane Taylor's 1806 lyric. Comfortably out of
# copyright everywhere TWANGA ships.
#
# Encoded as ASCII tab (the plain-text dashes-and-frets format on
# every tab-sharing site) for the ASCII parser fixture set. Standard
# 6-string guitar tuning — the parser should identify the labels
# against the built-in registry exactly and NOT emit an
# InferredTuning warning.
#
# Arrangement plays the melody on the first two strings only;
# the lower strings stay open / un-fretted, which is normal for
# how ASCII tabs notate single-string melodies.
#
# Fixture under MIT OR Apache-2.0.

e|--0--0--7--7--9--9--7-----|
B|--------------------------|
G|--------------------------|
D|--------------------------|
A|--------------------------|
E|--------------------------|
